  "patch": {
    "added": {
      "culvert_flushstop_test.go": "8fb7edadebe4ea0775ea95b21403b5066c70dd97872bbc08307da75eb76bd89f",
      "table/culvert_fileid_test.go": "21d9353e35a3dd5a3d4286055973ab6c2a487aa9a8ea3c79f3e975379c6fab3e"
    },
    "effect": "a failed memtable allocation (ensureRoomForWrite, dropAll, dropPrefixes) leaves the current memtable in place and returns the error instead of leaving db.mt nil (the next write was a fatal AssertTrue); a failed value-log grow returns the reserved offset (F-DISK-1); scanner fixes: memtable ids parse bounded to 31 bits (they become a uint32 WAL fid) and table ids parse as unsigned 32-bit below MaxUint32 (a negative, >= 2^32 or exactly MaxUint32 name is not a table file instead of a fatal AssertTrue), and Options log methods escape CR/LF (CWE-117); a flush that still fails when the flusher is asked to stop is no longer retried forever: on Close the memtables keep their WALs (synced, replayed on the next open) and Close returns that error; on a DropAll/DropPrefix pause they stay in db.imm and are re-queued in order when flushing resumes; a failed DropPrefix keeps db.imm consistent DropAll frees the immutable memtables, tables and value logs BEFORE allocating the replacement memtable, so a purge on a full filesystem frees the space instead of failing with ENOSPC before deleting anything (a failed allocation still keeps the current memtable).",
